      "message": "feat(ui): machined mesh paints deviation classes and lights the hovered facet\n\nThe extracted machined mesh (M13.1) now carries the Deviate legend:\neach facet is judged once per mesh by the GPU eye's own law - the\nmodel's DistanceLattice read at the facet centroid, gated by\ngate_tol(DEV_TOL, cell) - into clean / rest / gouge / unjudged\n(app::machined_classes, cached in MeshCache::classify next to the mesh,\nprimed with the extraction). The scene expands the classes to the stock\npart's per-vertex buffer, so the mesh paints the same colours as the\nsheet and the traced eye.\n\nA stock hover answered by the mesh keeps the triangle it hit\n(State::hover_mesh, view state, never a command); the shell draws it as\na hover-yellow veil and outline projected through the camera each frame.\n\nDecision: docs/decisions/25-mesh-hover-deviation.md\n\nFixes #25\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
